        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMost Cut 'n Sew instructions include a small seam allowance.  This would be equivalent to a surged edge.<br>\r\n\r\nBut what if you are knitting with a fine yarn?<br> The neckband could look limp, wimpy and look flimsy.  Plus you could clearly see a ridge created by the cut edge inside the band.<br>By wrapping the garment with the band, you will have a perfect band that is smooth and sturdy with no ridge showing.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/wrap1.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9580,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "873859561",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 9583,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Wrapped Neckband <span class=\"badge\">NEW</span>",
          "slug": "wrapped-neckband-span-class-badge-new-span",
          "order": 9,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6257,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .outlined-div {\r\n        border: 1px solid #000;\r\n        /* 1px solid border with black color (#000) */\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        /* 10px of padding inside the div */\r\nmargin: 10px;\r\n        /* Additional styles for your div can be added here */\r\n    }\r\n.yellow_highlight {\r\n\r\nbackground: linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0) 55%,#ffff00 45%,#ffff00);\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\nNeckbands can be constructed in 2 ways:\r\n\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"outlined-div\"><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>ONE PIECE BAND</b></span><br><i class=\"fa fa-check-circle-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Pro:</b></span><br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>\r\n                Less steps to knit <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">(easier of the 2 methods)</span></li>\r\n            <li>Finish on either the public or private side</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <i class=\"fa fa-check-circle-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Con:</b></span><br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>Finish on the private side isn't as neat (whip stitch)</li>\r\n            <li>Finish on the public side can be tedious to back stitch neatly</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <img class=\"img-thumbnail zoom\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/1 piece_compare.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"outlined-div\"><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>2 PIECE BAND </b></span><br><i class=\"fa fa-check-circle-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Pro:</b></span><br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>Both edges next to the garment are picked up and neat</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Collar or decorative finish can be added at the neck edge</span></li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <i class=\"fa fa-check-circle-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Con:</b></span><br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>Extra steps to create the band in 2 pieces</li>\r\n            <li>Extra care is needed to join the \"sandwich\"</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <img class=\"img-thumbnail zoom\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/compare2.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9591,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
