      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div class=\"text-center\"></div><br>\r\nIf you choose not to cut, the  Knit it Now Practice Neckline pattern is useful for the exercises in this workshop.  Combine practice with shaping necklines and adding bands. <br>You can choose to knit \"mini\" sizes to save time (and yarn) or full size necklines for practice.<br><a href=\"/knit/DynamicPattern/679/practice-necklines\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/practice1.jpg\"></a>\r\n<a href=\"/knit/DynamicPattern/679/practice-necklines\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/KIN_images/garments/practice_necklines400.jpg\"></a>\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9572,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Practice Pattern",
          "slug": "practice-pattern",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6249,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">Don't just watch videos, make time to practice the techniques suggested in this course.</span>",
              "legacyComponentId": 9570,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "exerciseAccordion",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\">Take the plunge ... cut some knitting</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n\r\nTake a blocked swatch in any stitch pattern and cut a curved edge.<br>Play with stretching and trying to make the stitches run.<br>\r\nObserve what happens<br>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/cut1.gif\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow1.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\">No stretching</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\nA key to success is to secure the knitting with minimal stretching or distortion of the knitting.<br>Consider using: \r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A Sewing machine walking foot</lil>\r\n<li>Your serger Differential Feed adjustment</li>\r\n<li>Sew with a paper backing (then remove the paper)</li>\r\n<li>\r\n\r\n <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Stabilizer for Cut \\'n Sew Excellence\" data-vimeoid=\"280094859\">Use   <i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><b> wash-away stablizer</b></div></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/stretch1.jpg\"><br><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/stretch2.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow2.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Exercise 1</b> One-piece fold over band</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "<style>\r\n    .outlined-div {\r\n        border: 1px solid #000;\r\n        /* 1px solid border with black color (#000) */\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> One-piece band - pick up practice</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 1 Part 1</h3>\r\n    <ol>\r\n        <li>Swatch and establish the gauge of your band in your desired stitch pattern (stockinette at first)</li>\r\n        <li>Knit or use a good size swatch and secure a round neck opening (zig zag or serger)</li>\r\n        <li>With the curved edge flat, use a tape measure and establish the length of the practice neck opening</li>\r\n        <li>Multiply the length by the band gauge</li>\r\n        <li><b>How many stitches do you need?</b></li>\r\n    </uol>\r\n</div><br>\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5em\">Don't forget to add seaming stitches!</span><br>\r\n<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> One-piece band - confirm pick up</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 1 Part 2</h3><br>\r\n    Hold the neck opening up to the needlebed and push it through the gate pegs (if you have them)\r\n\r\n    <b>How many needles will be used?</b><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> Knit a one-piece band</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 1 Part 3</h3><br>\r\n    <ol>\r\n        <li>\r\n            Hang the neckline:\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li>Right side facing - band will fold to the public side and stitches will be on the front of the garment</li>\r\n                <li>Wrong side facing - band will fold to the private side and stitches will be on the inside of the garment</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </li>\r\n        <li>\r\n            Knit a 1 piece band\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li>\r\n                    Grade the tension</li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                    Knit a <a data-GlossaryId='324' class='glossaryhelp'>Turning Row <i class='fa fa-question-circle' aria-hidden='true'></i></a></li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n\r\n        </li>\r\n        <li>Steam the band</li><br>\r\n        <li>Fold the band and stitch in place</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n</div>\r\n<Br>\r\n<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> Knit another one-piece band</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 1 Part 4</h3><br>\r\n    Repeat part 3, folding the band the other way (to the inside or outside)<br>\r\n    Stitching a band to the inside is easier (you don't have to be as precise) but stitching the band to the public side can be sooo worth the extra time and effort!\r\n    <br><span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5 em\">Practice a 1 piece band both ways .. you'll be glad you did!</span>\r\n</div>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow3.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Exercise 2 </b>Industrial 2 piece band</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> Knit an \"Industrial\" 2 piece band</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 2 Part 1</h3>\r\n    <ol>\r\n        <li>Swatch and establish the gauge of your band in your desired stitch pattern (stockinette at first)</li>\r\n        <li>Knit or use a good size swatch and secure a round neck opening (zig zag or serger)</li>\r\n        <li>With the curved edge flat, use a tape measure and establish the length of the practice neck opening</li>\r\n        <li>Multiply the length by the band gauge</li>\r\n        <li><b>How many stitches do you need?</b></li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n</div><br>\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5em\">Don't forget to add seaming stitches!</span><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n    <b> Knit an \"Industrial\" 2 piece band</b>\r\n    <h3>Exercise 2 Part 2</h3>\r\n    Follow this video <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Reversible Band\" data-vimeoid=\"223374072\"> <i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\"></i> Amazing Reversible band</div>\r\n    <ol>\r\n\r\n        <li>Scrap on (this will be the \"pick up\" edge)</li>\r\n        <li>Knit 1 half of the band</li>\r\n        <li>Grade (tighten) the tension</li>\r\n        <li>Scrap off (this edge will be the top of the band)</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n    Note the \"scrapped on\" edge will be picked up and attached to the body of the garment <br>\r\n    <b>TIP:</b> use different color scrap yarn to keep track\r\n    <br>\r\n\r\n    <ol start=\"5\">\r\n        <li>Pick up the garment edge (right or public side facing)</li>\r\n        <li>Rehang the band \"pick up\" edge (wrong side facing)</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n    <b>TIP:</b> Note the public sides of both pieces are facing each other\r\n    <ol start=\"7\">\r\n        <li>Pull the band stitches through the garment</li>\r\n        <li>Continue knitting the 2nd half of the band</li>\r\n        <li>Pick up the top edge of the first band section and loosely bind off (or Kitchener graft the 2 pieces)\r\n    </ol><br>\r\n</div><Br>\r\n    <div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n        <b> Knit another \"Industrial\" 2 piece band</b>\r\n        <h3>Exercise 2 Part 3</h3>\r\n\r\n        Repeat Parts 1 and 2 of this exercise, but instead of binding off, scrap off the 2nd band and <a data-GlossaryId='4704' class='glossaryhelp'>Kitchener graft<i class='fa fa-question-circle' aria-hidden='true'></i></a> the 2 band edges together for a seamless join.\r\n</div>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow4.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Exercise 3:</b> Industrial Rolled Edge</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"outlined-div\">\r\n\r\nRepeat the steps of Exercise 2 and knit a 2 piece band with a rolled edge<br>Watch this video  <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"rolled _edge_band\" data-vimeoid=\"345069044\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Cut 'n Sew Rolled Edge Band</div><br>before binding off or joining the 2 band pieces,  knit for 1/2 or desired number of rows for a rolled edge.<br>\r\n\r\n<b>TIP:</b> Knit the rolled edge in a contrasting color <br></div>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow5.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "<span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Exercise 4: </b>Stitch pattern challenge</span>",
                  "bodyHtml": "Choose the band method of your choice and knit the band in a stitch pattern at a different gauge than your garment.<br>Try:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Small fairisle</li>\r\n<li>Tuck</li>\r\n<li>Slip</li>\r\n<li>vertical stripes</li>\r\n<li> Contrasting color or different yarn weight</li\r\n</ul>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/116/arrow6.png"
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "showText": "below",
                "size": null
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 9571,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Don't Just Watch Videos!",
          "slug": "don-t-just-watch-videos",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6248,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n.lightlist ul { padding-left:20px; list-style:none; }\r\n.lightlist li { margin-bottom:10px; }\r\n.lightlist li:before {'FontAwesome';\r\ncontent: '\\f00c';\r\nmargin:0 5px 0 -15px;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:2em\"> ONE PIECE BAND</span>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"lightlist\" style=\"list-style:none;\"> \r\n<li>Join the shoulder(s)</li>\r\n<li>Cut 'n sew the garment edge</li>\r\n<li>Rehang the neck edge, stretching slightly</li>\r\n<li>Add a  marker row</li>\r\n<li>Manually knit 1 row with band yarn</li>\r\n<li>Knit 1/2 of the band (grading the tension)</li>\r\n<li>Knit a marker row</li>\r\n<li>Knit the second half of the band</li>\r\n<li>Scrap off</li>\r\n<li>Fold the band and stitch it in place</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/1 piece_compare.jpg\">\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:2em\"> TWO  PIECE BAND</span> (sandwich band)<br>\r\n<ul class=\"lightlist\" style=\"list-style:none;\"> \r\n<li>Join the shoulder(s)</li>\r\n<li>Cut 'n sew the garment edge</li>\r\n<li>Knit 1/2 of the band:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Scrap on</li>\r\n<li>Knit a row of ravel cord</li>\r\n<li>Knit 1/2 of the band depth (grading the tension)</li>\r\n<li>Scrap off</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Hang the neck edge, stretching slightly</li>\r\n<li>Re-hang the pre-knit band <b>from the scrapped off edge</b></li>\r\n<li>Pull the stitches through the knitting to join the band to the garment edge</li>\r\n<li>Knit the second band (grading the tension)</lil>\r\n<li>Join the 2 pieces with Kitchener stitch or bind off LOOSELY</li>\r\n<li>Remove the scrap yarn</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/116/compare2.jpg\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9590,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
